    <string name="disclosure_title">Accessibility service</string>
    <string name="disclosure_text_1">ZikrTime uses the accessibility service only to know which app is open. If it is a social app from your list and the limit is used up or it is prayer time, the app takes you to the home screen and shows a reminder.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_text_2">Screen content, messages and passwords are never read. Nothing is sent to the internet — everything stays on your phone.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_text_3">In settings, open \"Downloaded apps\" (or \"Installed services\") → ZikrTime and turn it on. If the switch is greyed out, open App info → menu ⋮ → \"Allow restricted settings\".</string>
